<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raúl Castro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1931">1931</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raúl Castro is a Cuban revolutionary and the younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a>. He fought in the 26th of July Movement and commanded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>'s armed forces for nearly fifty years. He succeeded Fidel as president in 2008 and as first secretary of the Communist Party in 2011, allowed limited market reforms, restored relations with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 2015 and retired in 2021.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raul-castro.jpg" alt="Raúl Castro" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Пресс-служба Президента России/ Presidential Executive Office Russia · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raul-castro-2015_(cropped)(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
